o  exit this level  um and making sure that you figure out  how to take down each of the  um  visionaries in a single loop  basically if you were trying to do that  with ai that would chase you down and  would hunt you down the same way that  they do in dishonored for example i  think that the the balance of the whole  game would be thrown off the game would  be nowhere near as good um it would it  would be frustrating uh a lot of people  would probably give up on trying to  solve the loop at all um which is  obviously your singular purpose in this  game it is not about trying to stealth  past enemies you can blow through  through them and i appreciate that about  this game that it plays differently  to um dishonest and certainly different  to pray too uh but what i wanted to talk  about today you know outside of having  said the things that i've already said  is  the  uh  parts of this discussion that i've seen  where people are essentially saying  the ai in this game is bad as though  arcane doesn't know how to make  a.i um  so for context and i i certainly assume  that this is the case with arcane as it  is for  every other video game that i'm aware of  uh  the ai knows where the player is 100 of  the time  that's that's your starting point the  the every single npc in the level every  single enemy that you're going to come  across knows where you are  100 of the time  the tweaking of that comes into play  with  i'm just going to do that run away again  i'm just gonna use this gameplay to  repeatedly show the issues  or the thing that i'm talking about  um  the balance is in actually dialing that  back and deciding the circumstances upon  which the ai will investigate where the  player is how they will react to the  player when they will engage in combat  when they will give up that's what is  actually the process it's not  none of these people have any idea where  cult is in the level and we need to move  that upwards in increments to make them  smarter it's actually that the ai is the  smartest knows absolutely everything is  running on the same code as cult and has  to be dialed and tweaked backwards and i  think that's the part of the  conversation that especially is someone  who very early mentioned issues with  the ai and thinking that some people  would find them to be uh dumb is that  it's not actually something that arcane  has done  by accident by any means  just not aiming at that very well  it is entirely  intentional um i feel like again  dishonest uh even frey  demonstrate that really well and that  you know they they do have ai that can  hunt you down it can be really really  punishing and can make it difficult to  get through things if you don't stealth  so what they've done here is go from the  100 that i'm talking about and dial it  um back not dial it forward they have  not made a mistake what they've done as  a studio who are  very good about creating uh punishing  stealth in other video games  is  change death loop to make it so that  they will be  pursuing you a lot less actively because  that is not the purpose of the game  um that is my main thesis here is that  while bad i think is again a word that i  use it's a really easy way to describe  this kind of ai meaning that you know  they're really easy to get away from  they don't act like people would you can  kill every single one of them without  too much of a challenge you can run away  you can duck behind a corner all of that  is is quite simple  the point is that they didn't do that by  creating dumb ai the ai is fantastic  and has been  reduced from 100 knowing where the  player is um to make sure that death  loop plays as the game it is intended to  be which is really  a smart puzzle game um it's a game where  you have to chase the breadcrumbs again  right now it's leading me towards the  exit figure out where everyone is  it is not a game about taking down every  npc to stealth your way through a level  like dishonored is so  it's it's very very very intentional  they've not made a mistake and so i  don't think the criticism is necessarily  fair  while yeah they are stupid  again it's not the right word  technically they're not stupid they know  exactly where you are and have a bunch  of contingencies to prevent them from  just trying to pursue you all the time  and it feels that way on a surface level  um i ultimately just think it's a very  basic criticism that that's  not to say that you know if you you wish  they were a little bit harder that i  think that that's invalid that's totally  fair but i'm just seeing people you know  use the words bad and dumb and stupid  as though arcane made a mistake but the  point that i'm trying to make is that  this is clearly really really really  really intentional um it is  the purpose  of the npcs in this game of the people  that i'm shooting throughout this video  with a tremendous amount of ease  they serve a very different purpose to  an ai in call of duty they serve a very  different purpose to  um enemy ai in again dishonored in prey  in in any of arcane's other works um and  the works of other stealth games as well  um and  while i would think the ai is not even  as difficult as hitman when you are  facing  uh such  a big through line i think even having  it be as aggressive as it is in hitman  which is you know not dissimilar in  terms of your inside of a sandbox trying  to follow the breadcrumbs that are  pretty readily handed out to you  um  hitman still feels really contained this  is one big picture and i just feel like  they they would have done the play  testing they would have done focus  testing even for this they would have  had people tinker with this over and  over and over again  to get to the point where it wasn't  incredibly frustrating for people to try  to solve the puzzle to try to focus on  the main story focus on the main quest  and actually  get through what is the purpose of the  game  um which yeah i imagine would have been  way way way too too difficult if it were  dishonest levels of difficult um  or dishonored levels of of  you know ai engagement ai pursuing you  um it's just a very different thing so  i i feel like it is yeah it's it's an  easy thing to say it's dumb thus the  game is bad but i think the reality is  actually the opposite is that the ai  is not aggressive in pursuing the player  because  arcane understands fundamentally what  the purpose of death loop is they want  to keep you on track with the purpose of  death loop as in following these leads  tracking down the visionaries and also  keeping the loops fun so that you're  still upgrading so that you can still  take out the visionaries um to upgrade  your nexus labs to upgrade your weapons  or whatever else  it's not dumb it is a very intentional  choice that makes the game satisfying to  play  that makes it fun for you to repeat  levels is probably the biggest thing  while there are in theory 16 maps  because of the day night cycle creating  you know 16 different  stages overall um and i feel like it's  so clear that that some of this design  uh for these levels came from um the  wolfenstein  uh game that they also worked on  um  yeah if if the ai were too aggressive  again there's no way they didn't balance  this and didn't think about this it's  not some programmer has made a mistake  um it was probably really frustrating to  get through them over and over and over  again and to to intentionally make some  of the mistakes that you are  sort of supposed to make  um and i have absolutely just just no  doubt that they knew that so i just  think we're kind of coming at it from  the wrong angle is sort of my point here  um i think that  it is  it is ai that was 100 aware of where the  player was  like you really should know where i am  and because they don't feel like the  behavior patterns of real people it just  it feels off and i'm not gonna yeah tell  anyone they're wrong for that criticism  but i do think the criticism is coming  from  the wrong place essentially  they they definitely know what they're  doing and have created a really balanced  game that i don't think feels  frustrating loot by loop that doesn't  get  um annoying because you're being killed  uh just for trying to figure out one  little tiny thing that that leads into  this bigger picture it is a very clear  balance from a studio who has definitely  made games where the ai is much much  much more punishing um it's supposed to  feel a lot more like your playground you  really are the main character of the  loop when you play as cult um  and yeah i think that's that's kind of  my point here is you know i feel like  we should maybe just have a little bit  more a little bit more faith yeah i  think i did use the word bad in my first  video  my point here is that i feel like bad is  a really reductive way to talk about  this and i probably shouldn't have used  the word bad but it also feels like such  an easy way to express the point of like  they don't react to you like real people  would  but that's not bad it is definitely  intentional and i think they've made the  right choice  uh overall i still think this game is  absolutely fantastic and yeah i just  wanted to make this quick video to talk  about that one particular thing because  i feel like so much of this conversation  specifically uh people are getting  caught up in um  at least in in some cases i'm definitely  not going to shoot this of everyone they  seem to assume that ai starts at zero  and then is slowly ramped up and that  they fail to ramp it up where actually  ai starts at 100 they know where the  player is 100 of the time  and you have to figure out how to layer  that backwards it's not the other way  around if that makes sense so  yeah i hope you guys enjoyed this video  i hope everything here uh makes sense  and i wasn't too rambly  [Laughter]  and i will see you guys next time bye

